	How about setting things up so that there are two sets of code running
when the game is being played.  The player code would handle only those things
that relate to that particular player - each person playing the game would run
his own player code process.  At the center of the game would be the dungeon 
code.  The first player to start a game would activate the dungeon code, and it
would remain active until the last player quits (exits/saves).

	Active levels would remain in memory under the dungeon process, and 
would go away when there were no longer any players on that level.  A level
that was active for a player that has saved his game will be kept until that
player resumes and leaves the level.  Of course, a player who leaves the game
saved runs the risk of the level being cleared out by the time he resumes.

	Opinions?
